f0985f5dd2 psbt: handle implicit taproot signature sighashes

Allow self-describing 65-byte taproot signatures when no per-input
sighash type and no explicit caller constraint were supplied.
Preserve strict matching when the caller or PSBT specifies a type.
Add parameterized regression coverage for both taproot signature forms.

8d161dbeef test: tighten PSBT sighash regression assertions

Require successful processing or the expected incomplete-signature result
instead of treating arbitrary errors as acceptance. Cover explicitly
requested non-default sighashes and mixed taproot script signatures.

95f024f692 test: cover explicit Taproot sighash without PSBT field

Use signatures generated by the wallet and descriptor signer to check
that a 65-byte Taproot key-path signature can be finalized when the
optional sighash field is absent. Check that a conflicting explicit
constraint remains rejected and that the finalized spend is valid.

2e977e45e7 test: exercise mixed Taproot script sighashes

Generate two independent signatures for a multi_a Taproot spend,
combine a default 64-byte signature and an explicit 65-byte signature,
and verify that finalization succeeds without an input sighash field.
Keep rejection for conflicting explicit input constraints.
